 dict(param='SCHOOL',score=2,stance='qualifies',key='veldhuisHistoryMesopotamianLexical2014',where='Veldhuis 2014 (GMTR 6), p. 64',
  quote="The Ur III period, which produced massive amounts of administrative texts, mainly from Puzriš-Dagan (Drehem), Umma, and Ĝirsu, has yielded very little lexical material. The scribes of the Ur III period must have been educated; there is good evidence that many of the Old Babylonian Sumerian literary texts were composed during the Ur III period and king Šulgi, in one of his hymns, famously takes credit for founding scribal schools at Nippur and Ur. All this educational and literary activity, however, has left few identifiable traces."),
