dict(param='SCHOOL', score=2, stance='qualifies', key='charpinReadingWriting2010', where='pp. 22-23', quote='But the creation of the edubba, literally, “the house of tablets,” must not be attributed to him, at least according to Hymn B, in which that king recalls the training he received in his childhood. In addition, the principal task Shulgi assigned to the edubba was not to train bureaucrats but to make copies of hymns', note='Šulgi reforms increased the number of administrative tablets and scribes (p. 22).'),
dict(param='STD', score=3, stance='supports', key='bartashEstablishingValueWeight2019', where='p. 110', quote="The Ur III system of weight measures and its notation in script has become a standard. Old Babylonian lexicographers introduced it in their compositions.", note='The prologue of the Laws of Ur-Namma (ll. 135-149) claims standardization of the sila, the mina and the shekel weights (p. 106).'),
dict(param='STD', score=2, stance='qualifies', key='bartashEstablishingValueWeight2019', where='pp. 105, 111', quote="the simplified Neo-Sumerian system of weight measures must have emerged in Sumer following the collapse of the Akkadian empire.", note='p. 111: Lagaš II Girsu "shows that we do not need to overrate the role of the centralized political power in the maintenance of metrology". The Ur III reform refined a system already in use.'),
dict(param='HIER', score=3, stance='supports', key='bartashEstablishingValueWeight2019', where='pp. 105-106', quote="For the first time, the state was divided into provinces where officials assigned by the crown, and not the local elites as in earlier times, played the first fiddle.", note='Summary statement in a metrology monograph; Ur III HIER is already well attested.'),
dict(param='TCTL', score=3, stance='supports', key='yoffeePoliticalEconomyEarly1995', where='p. 295', quote="Nevertheless, most of our documents come from royal archives or from temple archives that had been systematically placed under palace control during this period.", note=''),
