dict(param='PRIV', score=1, stance='qualifies', key='yoffeePoliticalEconomyEarly1995', where='p. 295', quote="There is additional evidence, however, of private sales, mainly of humans as slaves and of animals but also of house property and orchards (206).", note='Against the "enormous bureaucratic pyramid", which Yoffee says "must be substantially correct".'),
dict(param='BUR', score=3, stance='supports', key='yoffeePoliticalEconomyEarly1995', where='p. 295', quote="On large tablets, clerks added the daily receipts into six-monthly or yearly accounts. The tablets were stored in baskets equipped with tags (102). A system of double-entry bookkeeping was invented to manage the accounts", note='Puzriš-Dagan. Mentions tablet size by document level (daily vs. summary).'),
dict(param='SCHOOL', score=3, stance='supports', key='charpinHistoryAncientMesopotamia1995', where='p. 812', quote="It relied on a huge bureaucratic organization: scribes now received a uniform training that included new accounting procedures and new formats for archival texts. Such a degree of centralization was never achieved again, and ultimately the experiment failed.", note='Explicit link between uniform scribal training and new document formats.'),
